1
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,940
=When the Lights Rise=
=Episode 6=

2
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:25,740
Ding Zhao.

3
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:29,300
How did you get hurt?

4
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:31,340
Come in. Sit down.

5
00:01:32,660 --> 00:01:33,820
I'll tend to your wound.

6
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:34,570
Sit here.

7
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:41,900
You...

8
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:45,180
Didn't you take your sister
to the hospital?

9
00:01:45,180 --> 00:01:46,140
How did you end up like this?

10
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:47,620
She's missing.

11
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:48,420
Missing?

12
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:50,700
It's connected to Lv Mengde.

13
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:52,500
I went looking for her at Kaimeili,

14
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:53,940
but I couldn't find her.

15
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:02,220
It seems we're after the same thing now.

16
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:04,100
What do you mean?

17
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:07,220
Lisa, Kaimeili's most popular singer,

18
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:10,020
might be the person we're looking for.

19
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:21,740
Bear with me.

20
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:34,500
Who taught you?

21
00:02:35,980 --> 00:02:37,220
What?

22
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:42,900
Stitching wounds and making clothes.

23
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:46,580
Does that have anything
to do with our investigation?

24
00:02:47,260 --> 00:02:48,900
If we're going to work together,

25
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:51,820
we should get to know each other.

26
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:01,740
I learned from my family.

27
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:03,260
What about your parents?

28
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,260
That's personal.

29
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:08,140
It might be connected
to Mei Xiaozhu's death.

30
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:12,060
What are you getting at?

31
00:03:12,380 --> 00:03:15,860
Do you two have any other relatives?

32
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:23,220
When I was little,

33
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:26,860
my family came to Shanghai by boat
to make a living.

34
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:28,300
The boat capsized.

35
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:30,780
Only...

36
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:34,060
My sister and I survived.

37
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:37,740
After all these years,

38
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:40,180
I doubt we have any relatives left

39
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:41,500
worth keeping in touch with.

40
00:03:41,780 --> 00:03:42,580
That's good.

41
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:45,020
If we're going to keep investigating,

42
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:47,300
I hope

43
00:03:48,740 --> 00:03:49,420
neither of us

44
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:51,900
will have any more family members
dragged into this.

45
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:23,020
Boss Ding, looking for some fun

46
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:24,820
in broad daylight?

47
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:26,900
Business doesn't seem
to be going well for you either.

48
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:28,540
As long as you repay your debts on time,

49
00:04:28,620 --> 00:04:30,420
we can stay in business.

50
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:31,620
Isn't that right?

51
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:34,820
How about I repay you another way?

52
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:39,420
You're quite unusual, Boss Ding.

53
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,460
Bringing a woman along to collect debts.

54
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:43,140
We're not here to collect debts.

55
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:44,740
We're looking
for information about a girl.

56
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:45,660
Information?

57
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:47,580
This is Fourth Road.

58
00:04:47,660 --> 00:04:49,220
Some people are fair game for questions,

59
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:51,020
but others are off-limits.

60
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:54,920
We'll leave as soon
as we've asked our questions.

61
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,460
We won't interfere with your business.

62
00:04:57,460 --> 00:04:58,740
Do you know Mei Xiaozhu?

63
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:06,380
Every time that girl left Kaimeili,

64
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:08,060
a woman would come to pick her up.

65
00:05:08,980 --> 00:05:11,820
She'd sit in a rickshaw
some distance away.

66
00:05:12,060 --> 00:05:15,300
And she was dressed
in incredibly expensive clothes.

67
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:19,460
But no one ever saw her face.

68
00:05:21,460 --> 00:05:22,980
She kept her face hidden.

69
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:24,660
Lisa is famous,

70
00:05:24,780 --> 00:05:26,020
so she could be the one.

71
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:28,660
But the timing doesn't match
when Xiaozhu went home.

72
00:05:29,020 --> 00:05:30,620
Lisa couldn't have been
performing onstage

73
00:05:30,620 --> 00:05:31,740
and picking up Xiaozhu at the same time.

74
00:05:32,620 --> 00:05:33,780
That's strange.

75
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:34,980
If it wasn't her,

76
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:36,580
who could this older woman be?

77
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:38,860
A week before Xiaozhu's death,

78
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:40,780
Lisa announced she was leaving Kaimeili

79
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:42,020
to marry into a wealthy family.

80
00:05:43,020 --> 00:05:44,420
The dance hostess just said

81
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:46,700
Lisa hasn't performed there
for two weeks.

82
00:05:49,460 --> 00:05:50,300
What do you think?

83
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:55,060
Whoever this woman is,

84
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:57,180
wherever she came from
to get to Kaimeili,

85
00:05:58,060 --> 00:05:59,540
she must have returned there afterward.

86
00:06:14,020 --> 00:06:14,820
What's wrong?

87
00:06:15,260 --> 00:06:16,100
Boss,

88
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:18,580
I really can't run any farther.

89
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:20,060
This place is too far.

90
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:22,740
We've crossed an entire district.

91
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:25,260
Do people usually ask you
to come this far?

92
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:26,220
Not very often.

93
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:28,540
This place is too remote.

94
00:06:28,940 --> 00:06:29,740
Thank you.

95
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:31,620
Thank you, sir.

96
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:32,500
Thank you, sir.

97
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:41,420
Well?

98
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:42,460
Found anything?

99
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:47,980
This street...

100
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:50,940
Go to the end of this street,

101
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:51,620
then turn right,

102
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:52,980
and you'll reach your tailor shop.

103
00:06:53,380 --> 00:06:54,900
Judging by how far
the rickshaw driver could travel,

104
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:56,860
if she was taking Xiaozhu home,

105
00:06:57,420 --> 00:06:59,100
she must have dropped her off
somewhere nearby.

106
00:07:06,820 --> 00:07:07,410
No.

107
00:07:10,340 --> 00:07:11,060
What's wrong?

108
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:12,820
Get me some hot water.

109
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:13,860
I want to wash my face.

110
00:07:16,940 --> 00:07:17,740
Hot water.

111
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:19,620
Hot water?

112
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:21,120
You didn't know
she frequented nightclubs,

113
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,120
which means she must have had somewhere

114
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:23,780
to wash up and change clothes
before coming home.

115
00:07:25,660 --> 00:07:26,460
You're back.

116
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:27,540
Why are you home so late?

117
00:07:29,780 --> 00:07:30,660
Didn't you take an umbrella?

118
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:32,060
How did your hair get wet?

119
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:33,020
Where have you been?

120
00:07:33,060 --> 00:07:34,100
A classmate's birthday party.

121
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:36,300
You mean

122
00:07:37,020 --> 00:07:38,740
that woman lives nearby?

123
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:39,620
No.

124
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:43,340
The French Concession has strict checks
on property sales and rentals.

125
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:45,100
If she lived nearby,

126
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:47,100
Lv Mengde would have found her.

127
00:07:47,990 --> 00:07:50,780
Could she have stayed
at a hotel or somewhere similar?

128
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:52,220
She only needed to wash up.

129
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:53,220
She wouldn't need to stay overnight.

130
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:55,140
If my guess is right,

131
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:57,180
she'd have to go
from Fourth Road to Minguo Road,

132
00:07:57,620 --> 00:07:58,620
enter the concessions,

133
00:07:58,820 --> 00:08:00,460
and stay close to your shop.

134
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:02,340
There's only one place

135
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:03,900
that meets all those conditions.

136
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:07,140
A hot water shop.

137
00:08:07,660 --> 00:08:08,760
We have hot water here.

138
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:09,460
You can take a bath.

139
00:08:09,460 --> 00:08:10,460
We also have beds.

140
00:08:10,700 --> 00:08:13,020
It's much cheaper
than a bathhouse or hotel.

141
00:08:13,020 --> 00:08:13,820
You two,

142
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:15,340
which room would you like?

143
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:17,300
Excuse me, I'd like to ask something.

144
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:18,940
Have any young girls been here?

145
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:21,780
Young girls?

146
00:08:21,820 --> 00:08:22,740
A pair of sisters?

147
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:25,180
Plenty of women come here for hot water.

148
00:08:25,750 --> 00:08:27,430
Young girls...

149
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:28,820
Do you mean two

150
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:29,900
pretty,

151
00:08:30,020 --> 00:08:32,300
well-dressed young women?

152
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:33,200
One wore a qipao,

153
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,240
and the other wore a Western-style dress?

154
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:35,060
Yes, that's right.

155
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:37,860
Oh, you're asking about them.

156
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:39,860
They used to come here quite often.

157
00:08:39,860 --> 00:08:41,500
The older one looked a few years older.

158
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:43,560
The younger one looked like a student.

159
00:08:44,060 --> 00:08:45,460
They looked quite alike.

160
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:47,060
Very much alike.

161
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:48,300
When did they come?

162
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:49,300
Do you keep records?

163
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:52,140
Why would a shabby place
like ours keep records?

164
00:08:52,860 --> 00:08:53,420
Last night,

165
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:54,940
the older one came by.

166
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:55,740
She did?

167
00:08:55,860 --> 00:08:56,660
Last night?

168
00:08:56,900 --> 00:08:57,940
Did she come for a bath?

169
00:08:58,420 --> 00:08:59,420
That's the strange part.

170
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:01,820
She asked for the room
they usually used.

171
00:09:02,130 --> 00:09:03,220
She didn't ask for hot water

172
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:04,220
or take a bath.

173
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:06,060
She just stayed
in the room briefly and left.

174
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:06,820
Which room?

175
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:08,020
That one over there.

176
00:09:17,220 --> 00:09:19,580
What do you think
that woman came here for yesterday?

177
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:20,860
It seems she came to collect something.

178
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:21,940
Collect something?

179
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:24,300
I'm afraid we're too late.

180
00:09:41,620 --> 00:09:42,420
Here it is.

181
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:47,020
Lisa.

182
00:09:47,020 --> 00:09:47,840
(Mei Xiaozhu, Dong Zhenglun,
Lisa, Kong Shun)

183
00:09:49,980 --> 00:09:52,460
Kong Shun, Director Kong
of the Civil Affairs Bureau.

184
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:54,740
What do you think this is?

185
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:57,100
It looks like some kind of mark.

186
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:58,300
Xiaozhu.

187
00:09:58,300 --> 00:09:59,280
(Mei Xiaozhu, Dong Zhenglun)

188
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:00,880
(Dong Zhenglun)

189
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:02,140
Dong...

190
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:05,540
Are you all right?

191
00:10:09,020 --> 00:10:09,820
No.

192
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:12,900
And I won't let them get away with this.

193
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:35,500
Coca leaves.

194
00:10:42,620 --> 00:10:43,940
At 12 o'clock tonight.

195
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:46,420
Meet me at the tram stop
on Joffre Avenue.

196
00:10:58,340 --> 00:10:59,300
Joffre Avenue.

197
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:00,220
Time to get off.

198
00:11:07,460 --> 00:11:08,820
Get on. Sit properly.

199
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:10,540
Routine inspection.

200
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:38,420
Boss, we need to get out of here.

201
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:01,260
Are you all right?

202
00:13:02,540 --> 00:13:03,340
Let's go.

203
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:15,460
What are you doing?

204
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:17,860
They came to collect something.

205
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:20,020
Hurry up!

206
00:13:20,020 --> 00:13:21,480
We won't be able to explain ourselves
when the police arrive.

207
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:22,820
What they took was drugs, wasn't it?

208
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:24,100
Let's go. Come on.

209
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:37,940
A Kuang family car.

210
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:02,540
Boss.

211
00:14:03,060 --> 00:14:04,180
The goods are indeed gone.

212
00:14:10,980 --> 00:14:11,700
Head back.

213
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:12,380
Yes.

214
00:14:15,180 --> 00:14:16,780
The Kuang family is using
the docks to transport goods,

215
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:18,660
then hiding them inside trams

216
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:19,780
to get past checkpoints

217
00:14:20,020 --> 00:14:21,020
and bring them into the concessions.

218
00:14:24,060 --> 00:14:25,580
That's what you touched earlier.

219
00:14:25,620 --> 00:14:26,500
What was it?

220
00:14:27,420 --> 00:14:28,300
Black powder.

221
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:38,940
How do you explain

222
00:14:39,180 --> 00:14:40,220
tonight's hijacking of the shipment?

223
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:43,740
Father, you suspect me?

224
00:14:44,780 --> 00:14:45,580
Mengde.

225
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:48,380
Now that I've welcomed you back
into the Kuang family,

226
00:14:48,820 --> 00:14:49,980
everything I own

227
00:14:50,060 --> 00:14:51,420
will eventually be yours.

228
00:14:51,620 --> 00:14:53,060
Using our docks

229
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:55,700
to transport a little
merchandise of your own

230
00:14:56,420 --> 00:14:57,620
wouldn't have been a problem.

231
00:14:57,860 --> 00:14:59,420
But you shouldn't have kept it from me.

232
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:00,740
I don't know what
you're talking about, Father.

233
00:15:00,740 --> 00:15:02,620
You smuggled black powder into Shanghai.

234
00:15:02,620 --> 00:15:03,940
This is no small matter.

235
00:15:05,620 --> 00:15:06,500
As for the police,

236
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:08,220
I've already settled things with them.

237
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:09,900
But the chief inspector's demand

238
00:15:09,980 --> 00:15:10,820
is simple.

239
00:15:11,460 --> 00:15:13,740
Ten thousand silver dollars
for each life.

240
00:15:14,780 --> 00:15:16,300
Four officers died tonight.

241
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:20,100
Send them forty thousand
silver dollars later.

242
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:22,380
That will settle the matter.

243
00:15:22,620 --> 00:15:23,860
What's that got to do with me?

244
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:25,860
Why should I pay?

245
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:27,900
You know perfectly well why.

246
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:29,060
I have no idea.

247
00:15:29,860 --> 00:15:30,540
Father.

248
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:32,340
The docks are yours.

249
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:34,500
The goods are yours.

250
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:36,580
You tipped off the police.

251
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:38,140
You're the one who got those men killed.

252
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:39,420
No matter how

253
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:40,540
this matter is investigated,

254
00:15:41,060 --> 00:15:42,540
I don't see how it could
lead back to me.

255
00:15:42,820 --> 00:15:44,460
I'm trying to clean up your mess.

256
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:46,260
- Do you understand?
- You're not cleaning up my mess.

257
00:15:46,260 --> 00:15:47,620
You're using me!

258
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:49,060
What kind of nonsense is that?

259
00:15:56,020 --> 00:15:56,700
Father.

260
00:15:57,740 --> 00:15:59,240
It's not right to turn your back
on someone who's helped you.

261
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:04,100
You wanted to save
the family's tobacco shops.

262
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:05,940
That's why I introduced you
to the smuggled liquor business.

263
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:06,940
And look what happened.

264
00:16:06,980 --> 00:16:08,220
Now you're blaming me
when things go wrong.

265
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:10,220
How am I blaming you?

266
00:16:10,380 --> 00:16:11,620
Weren't you the one
who brought in the gunpowder?

267
00:16:11,620 --> 00:16:12,420
Does that matter?

268
00:16:17,580 --> 00:16:18,300
Father.

269
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:20,860
If Boss Ren hears about this,

270
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:23,300
do you think

271
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:27,780
he'll believe I was responsible?

272
00:16:30,020 --> 00:16:31,140
Smuggling weapons

273
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:33,780
cuts into his profits.

274
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:36,700
You ungrateful brat.

275
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:38,820
How dare you scheme against me?

276
00:16:39,020 --> 00:16:40,060
I'm your son, Father.

277
00:16:40,060 --> 00:16:41,380
Why would I scheme against you?

278
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:42,540
Then what exactly do you want?

279
00:16:43,260 --> 00:16:44,220
Forty thousand silver dollars.

280
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:46,140
You pay.

281
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:47,220
I...

282
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:50,660
Right now, the family

283
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:52,780
simply doesn't have that much cash.

284
00:16:53,660 --> 00:16:54,380
Then

285
00:16:57,460 --> 00:16:58,940
have my eldest sister step in

286
00:16:59,660 --> 00:17:03,100
and make a gesture of goodwill
to Boss Ren and the Kun Society.

287
00:17:03,380 --> 00:17:03,820
You...

288
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:04,940
She...

289
00:17:05,180 --> 00:17:06,900
What can a woman like her possibly do?

290
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:08,420
Father, don't you know?

291
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:11,300
The head
of the Japanese Chamber of Commerce,

292
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:12,740
Mr. Yoshida,

293
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:15,460
is very fond of my eldest sister.

294
00:17:17,260 --> 00:17:18,100
And he

295
00:17:18,860 --> 00:17:21,300
is Boss Ren's most important client.

296
00:17:23,100 --> 00:17:24,700
As for bringing people together,

297
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:26,220
Father...

298
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:27,340
You...

299
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:30,300
You want your sister to remarry?

300
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:33,020
Father.

301
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:34,780
You're getting confused in your old age.

302
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:36,500
How old is my eldest sister now?

303
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:40,380
I just mean that
when he comes to Shanghai,

304
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:42,900
my sister should spend
more time with him.

305
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:44,180
You...

306
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:45,180
Come on, Father.

307
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:46,500
Sit down. Sit.

308
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:47,300
Sit.

309
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:51,220
Father.

310
00:17:52,060 --> 00:17:53,380
Haven't you always thought

311
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:55,380
my brother-in-law was useless

312
00:17:55,620 --> 00:17:56,980
and never did anything
for the Kuang family?

313
00:17:58,020 --> 00:17:59,260
Now that he's dead,

314
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:00,340
shouldn't my sister

315
00:18:01,060 --> 00:18:02,020
do something

316
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:04,660
for the Kuang family?

317
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:30,660
As for the black powder,

318
00:18:32,860 --> 00:18:34,100
I'll find a way to handle it.

319
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:41,520
♪And watch the lights
come on one by one♪

320
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:44,920
♪Like blades cutting
through the radiance♪

321
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:48,400
♪You may treat me as dust
beneath your feet♪

322
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:50,320
♪Or wipe me away like ashes♪

323
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:51,880
♪Leaving a cold ending♪

324
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:53,840
♪But I refuse to fall♪

325
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:58,760
♪I refuse to become a shadow
fading beneath the lights♪

326
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:01,320
♪I refuse to dissolve into♪

327
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:05,400
♪The lifeless light of the past♪

328
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:08,560
♪I want sharpness at my fingertips♪

329
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:11,400
♪And steps that avoid
the traps among the thorns♪

330
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:15,000
♪At dawn, I will look
straight into your eyes♪

331
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:18,200
♪My gaze clear, illuminating the dawn♪

332
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:22,440
♪Those who have hurt me♪

333
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,680
♪I choose to pierce through♪

334
00:19:27,280 --> 00:19:28,760
♪To tear apart♪

335
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:34,760
♪To ignite a sacred flame♪

336
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:38,560
♪I do not pray to the gods♪

337
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:41,480
♪Nor bow to power♪

338
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:43,760
♪I will no longer play the tragic lead♪

339
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:49,480
♪I will stand and carve
the path of my own fate♪
